From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abe Massry <amassry@linode.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:34:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] accel/tcg: run the vCPU inline from the main loop on WASI

WASI has no threads (pthread_create() is a stub that never runs the
thread), so the round-robin vCPU cannot have a thread of its own.
Instead the main loop runs it for a time slice on each iteration,
through wasi_rr_cpu_step().

- tcg-accel-ops-rr.c: do rr_cpu_thread_fn()'s setup inline, record the
  one thread as the vCPU thread so that qemu_cpu_is_self() holds
  (otherwise apic_update_irq() kicks the vCPU forever), and add
  wasi_rr_cpu_step().  The thread is already an RCU reader.
- tcg-all.c: no MTTCG; there is a single thread.
- cpu-exec.c: as no timer thread kicks the vCPU, return to the main
  loop periodically so that timers, and the IRQs they raise, are
  serviced.  A busy guest's timer tick is due at nearly every return,
  and a tick costs it a couple of thousand TBs, so slices are timed
  (QEMU_TB_SLICE_MS, default 30 ms): with slices of 4000 TBs, ticks
  took about half of the guest's time.
- cputlb.c: let I/O accesses proceed instead of retranslating a
  single-instruction TB (cpu_io_recompile()), which never converged
  here; without icount the exact instruction boundary is not needed.
- cpus.c, cpu-common.c: stop the vCPU, and run run_on_cpu() work,
  directly; there is no other thread to wait for.
- tcg-cpu-ops.h: no _Noreturn on the do_unaligned_access pointer, as
  C11 does not allow it on function pointers.

Debugging aids, off unless their environment variable is set:
QEMU_DUMP_AT=<pc>,<n>,<addr>,<len>,<path> dumps guest memory and the
CPU state on the n-th run of a TB; QEMU_LOOP_DIAG=1 turns on TCG
logging when the same TB runs a million times in a row; the
QEMU_STATUS_EVERY report includes the most recently executed TBs.
